Theoretically it's up to the patch writer to decide how their changes
should be activated -- the choices include having them active by default,
using a runtime option in your config-file or with the 'O' command,
and using a compile time option. Many do the latter.

So what you should do is read the documentation that comes with the
patch.  Some provide documentation in separate files, some patch into the
guidebook. Visiting the site you mentioned above and taking a quick look
at the first patch you mentioned, splittable #adjust, I notice it says
quite clearly, in the patch description of the download page, that you
should add a '#define ADJSPLIT' line into include/config.h before compiling.

